Make the yanglint tcltest suites run without a controlling terminal

The SONiC build runs every package recipe with stdin redirected from
/dev/null and stdout piped to the log, and the slave container has no
controlling terminal. Under those conditions the libyang test harness
had two problems:

1. tests/tool_i.tcl registered its `expect_after { eof ... timeout ... }`
   before any `spawn`, which binds the patterns to Expect's stdin/stdout
   channel. With stdin at EOF the `eof` branch fires immediately in the
   first test of every file, and Expect closes its stdin/stdout pair on
   the way, so tcltest then dies with
   `error writing "stdout": bad file number`. Bind the patterns to the
   spawn ids of the running `expect` command instead.

2. tests/yanglint/interactive/ly.tcl set the width with `stty columns
   720`, which acts on the controlling terminal. Without one the spawned
   pty keeps 0 columns, so yanglint's line editor sends a cursor
   position query and waits forever for an answer. Use Expect's
   `stty_init`, which is applied to the new pty by `spawn` itself.

3. all.tcl only propagated failed tests to the exit code. A test file that
   fails to run at all (as in 1.) is reported by tcltest as a file-level
   error, not counted in numTests, so the suite exited 0 after executing
   zero tests and ctest reported it as Passed. Propagate the return value
   of tcltest::runAllTests, which is true when a file failed to run.

Result in the SONiC build: yanglint_interactive goes from
"Total 0 Passed 0" with 18 file-level errors to "Total 116 Passed 114
Skipped 2 Failed 0" (the 2 skips carry the `!ctest` constraint).

kamelnetworks/sonic-buildimage#50

diff --git a/tests/tool_i.tcl b/tests/tool_i.tcl
index fa8c964..5446969 100644
--- a/tests/tool_i.tcl
+++ b/tests/tool_i.tcl
@@ -30,7 +30,11 @@ set error_prompt ">>>"
 set error_head "$error_prompt Check-failed"
 
 # detection on eof and timeout will be on every expect command
-expect_after {
+# Bind the patterns to the spawn ids of the expect command being executed,
+# not to the spawn id current at this point (the user's stdin/stdout).
+# Otherwise an EOF on stdin, as when the tests run with stdin redirected
+# from /dev/null, matches immediately and also closes stdout.
+expect_after -i $any_spawn_id {
     eof {
         global error_head
         error "$error_head unexpected termination"
diff --git a/tests/yanglint/interactive/all.tcl b/tests/yanglint/interactive/all.tcl
index b22a5ab..5d723d8 100644
--- a/tests/yanglint/interactive/all.tcl
+++ b/tests/yanglint/interactive/all.tcl
@@ -11,5 +11,10 @@ if {[info exists ::env(TESTS_DIR)]} {
     tcltest::configure -testdir "$env(TESTS_DIR)/interactive"
 }
 
-tcltest::runAllTests
+set rc [tcltest::runAllTests]
+# runAllTests returns true if a test file failed to run at all (for example
+# an error outside of a test); such files are not counted in numTests.
+if {$rc ne "" && $rc} {
+    set exitCode 1
+}
 exit $exitCode
diff --git a/tests/yanglint/interactive/ly.tcl b/tests/yanglint/interactive/ly.tcl
index efa57f2..83c4d24 100644
--- a/tests/yanglint/interactive/ly.tcl
+++ b/tests/yanglint/interactive/ly.tcl
@@ -13,8 +13,12 @@ set timeout 5
 set prompt "> "
 # turn off dialog between expect and yanglint
 log_user 0
-# setting some large terminal width
-stty columns 720
+# setting some large terminal width for the spawned pty
+# (stty_init is applied by spawn to the new pty itself, so it works without
+# a controlling terminal; "stty columns" would only change the controlling
+# terminal and leave the pty with 0 columns, which makes yanglint query the
+# cursor position and wait forever for an answer)
+set stty_init "columns 720"
 
 # default setup for every unit test
 variable ly_setup {
diff --git a/tests/yanglint/non-interactive/all.tcl b/tests/yanglint/non-interactive/all.tcl
index 998c03a..639f1b4 100644
--- a/tests/yanglint/non-interactive/all.tcl
+++ b/tests/yanglint/non-interactive/all.tcl
@@ -11,5 +11,10 @@ if {[info exists ::env(TESTS_DIR)]} {
     tcltest::configure -testdir "$env(TESTS_DIR)/non-interactive"
 }
 
-tcltest::runAllTests
+set rc [tcltest::runAllTests]
+# runAllTests returns true if a test file failed to run at all (for example
+# an error outside of a test); such files are not counted in numTests.
+if {$rc ne "" && $rc} {
+    set exitCode 1
+}
 exit $exitCode
